hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1146","It was narrated by Muhammad bin Bashar, it was narrated by Muhammad bin Jaafar, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, he said: I bear witness to my father. Hurairah and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri that they bore witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “God gives a third of the night to pass.” So he comes down and says: Is there anyone who is repenting? Is there anyone seeking forgiveness for a sin? Then a man said to him: Until the beginning of dawn? He said: “Yes.”"
"1147","Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, Abu Yahya told me and he is Sulaym bin Amir, Damra bin Habib, and Abu Talha is Nu’aym bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, who said: Amr bin told me Anbasa, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was staying in Ukaz, and he mentioned the hadith, and said: So I said: O Messenger of God! Is there one call sooner than another, or an hour earlier? He said: “Yes, the closest the Lord comes to the servant is in the middle of the night, so if you are able to be among those who remember God at that hour, then be.”"
